<td id="S5.T2.5.1.12.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;"><span id="S5.T2.5.1.12.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.15</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.5.1.12.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;"><span id="S5.T2.5.1.12.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1.15</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">V-E</span> </span><span id="S5.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Parameter Tuning</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This procedure analyzes exponent statistics to derive parameters that minimize the average compressed bit-length under a specialized cost model, following systematic phases:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase 1: Statistical Pre-Analysis.</span> The initial phase involves constructing a histogram of the exponents extracted from the source data to obtain a frequency distribution for each unique exponent <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. This distribution allows for the calculation of the probability <math id="S5.SS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)</annotation></semantics></math> of each value occurring and the identification of the global minimum (<math id="S5.SS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>) and maximum (<math id="S5.SS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>) values in the exponents.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase 2: Global Search for a Suitable Linear Mapping Parameter (<math id="S5.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>) and Base Bit-Width (<math id="S5.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>).</span> The algorithm performs an exhaustive search for a linear mapping parameter <math id="S5.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> across its feasible integer domain. For each candidate <math id="S5.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, the requisite base bit-width <math id="S5.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is computed as the minimal number of bits required to span the data range relative to <math id="S5.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S5.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\footnotesize n=\max\left(\lfloor\log_{2}(b-l)\rfloor+1,\lceil\log_{2}(h-b)\rceil\right)+1" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">b</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">l</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">log</mi><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">h</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">b</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\footnotesize n=\max\left(\lfloor\log_{2}(b-l)\rfloor+1,\lceil\log_{2}(h-b)\rceil\right)+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b,n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b,n)</annotation></semantics></math> pair, all original exponents <math id="S5.SS5.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> are transformed via a mapping:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S5.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\footnotesize y=(2^{n}-x+b)\%{2^{n}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><mi mathsize="0.800em">n</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">b</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn mathsize="0.800em">2</mn><mi mathsize="0.800em">n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\footnotesize y=(2^{n}-x+b)\%{2^{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">A cost function <math id="S5.SS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, defined as the probability-weighted sum of the transformed values, is evaluated:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S5.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\footnotesize D=\sum_{x}p(x)\cdot y" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">D</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi></munder><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">x</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\footnotesize D=\sum_{x}p(x)\cdot y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The pair <math id="S5.SS5.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b^{*},n^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b^{*},n^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> that results in the minimum value for <math id="S5.SS5.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is selected. Using the selected parameters <math id="S5.SS5.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(b^{*},n^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(b^{*},n^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, the original exponents are transformed via Equation <a href="#S5.E2" title="In V-E Parameter Tuning ‣ V Optimizations of ENEC ‣ ENEC: A Lossless AI Model Compression Method Enabling Fast Inference on Ascend NPUs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. A statistical analysis of the bit-widths required for the transformed values <math id="S5.SS5.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is then performed. This yields the cumulative distribution function <math id="S5.SS5.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(m)</annotation></semantics></math>, representing the probability that a value <math id="S5.SS5.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> can be represented using <math id="S5.SS5.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> or fewer bits.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase 3: Selection of Encoding Threshold (<math id="S5.SS5.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>) and Group Length (<math id="S5.SS5.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>).</span> In the final phase, the appropriate encoding threshold <math id="S5.SS5.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and group length <math id="S5.SS5.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> are determined. Both <math id="S5.SS5.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS5.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> are treated as parameters. Since Ascend NPUs require data movement to be 32-byte aligned, we must set L <math id="S5.SS5.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS5.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>. The final parameter pair is selected through a joint search to minimize the expected bit length <math id="S5.SS5.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mtext>exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\footnotesize(m^{*},L^{*})=\min_{m,L}\left[B_{\text{exp}}=\frac{1}{L}+n+(m-n)\cdot p(m)^{L}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">∗</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><munder><mi mathsize="0.800em">min</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.800em">B</mi><mtext mathsize="0.800em">exp</mtext></msub><mo mathsize="0.800em">=</mo><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.800em">1</mn><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.800em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">n</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.800em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">p</mi><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.800em">m</mi><mo maxsize="0.800em" minsize="0.800em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.800em">L</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\footnotesize(m^{*},L^{*})=\min_{m,L}\left[B_{\text{exp}}=\frac{1}{L}+n+(m-n)\cdot p(m)^{L}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Under parameters <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,L)</annotation></semantics></math>, expected bits per element <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math> comprises amortized group mask overhead <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, base bit-width <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, and threshold effect <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-n)\cdot p(m)^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-n)\cdot p(m)^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. For such groups, each element uses <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> bits, saving <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-m</annotation></semantics></math> per element, giving expected saving <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-m)\cdot p(m)^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-m)\cdot p(m)^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> or equivalently adding <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-n)\cdot p(m)^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-n)\cdot p(m)^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> to baseline <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. Optimal <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m^{*},L^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m^{*},L^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> minimize <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\text{exp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\text{exp}}</annotation></semantics></math> by balancing: larger <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> reduces <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{L}</annotation></semantics></math> but lowers <math id="S5.SS5.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(m)^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(m)^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Upon completion of this process, the algorithm outputs the best set of selected parameters, denoted as the chosen linear mapping parameter <math id="S5.SS5.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, the base bit-width <math id="S5.SS5.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, the encoding threshold <math id="S5.SS5.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the group length <math id="S5.SS5.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VI </span><span id="S6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experimental Evaluation</span></h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Platforms.</span>
<span id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
All evaluations of NPU-based methods are performed on the Ascend NPU 910B2, which contains 24 Cube Units and 48 Vector Units (with a vector-to-cube unit ratio of 2:1). The host machine is powered by a HiSilicon Kunpeng-920 CPU running Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS, with NPU driver version 25.0.rc1.1. Our algorithms are implemented in C++17 using the AscendC framework, with toolkit version 8.2.RC1.alpha002 and the same version for the operator kernel package. To ensure a fair comparison, CPU-based and GPU-based methods are evaluated on a performance-similar<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2</span></span>
              
              
              
            <span id="footnote2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A800 tensor core vs 910B2 cube<span id="footnote2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: peak TF32: 156 vs 176 TFLOPS; peak FP16/BF16: 312 vs 353 TFLOPS.
<br class="ltx_break"></span>A800 CUDA core vs 910B2 vector<span id="footnote2.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: peak FP32: 19.5 vs 11 TFLOPS; peak FP16: 78 vs 22 TFLOPS; peak BF16: 39 vs 22 TFLOPS.
<br class="ltx_break"></span>A800 vs 910B2 HBM bandwidth<span id="footnote2.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: 1.5 vs 1.6 TB/s.</span></span></span></span></span> NVIDIA A800 GPU platform, which is equipped with Intel Xeon 8358P CPUs and uses CUDA version 12.6.
</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">TABLE III</span>: </span><span id="S6.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Popular models’ weights data used in this work.</span></figcaption>
